+// dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2 client plane:
+//   * The 0.1.0-era client aggregation package was removed in alpha.1 (API-10);
+//     do not reintroduce it in peers, dsh.client.inject, or an import. The
+//     client context type is the Cordis `Context`; every ctx facet comes from
+//     its owning package and is pulled into the type graph by the type-only
+//     imports in client.d.ts (and the JSDoc typedefs below):
+//       ctx.slots / SlotRegistry — @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-renderer/client
+//       settings.section SlotMap — @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-settings/client
+//       ctx.locale               — @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-locale/client
+//   * `ctx.slots` is provided by the ui-renderer browser half, NOT by
+//     ui-slots (ui-slots is the renderer-independent pure core and is seeded
+//     as a static platform module).
+//   * This file is the client module system's lazy-CJS factory artifact, not an
+//     ES module. The combo route serves these exact bytes as a classic script,
+//     so the bundle registers its factory through window.__ModuleLoader__.load
+//     under the boot graph row id — the package.json `name` (DSH-0.1.2-A1-26:
+//     entry name == package name == registration id). A bare `import`/`export`
+//     would be a classic-script SyntaxError, so type-only references live in
+//     JSDoc plus client.d.ts and every runtime module request goes through the
+//     factory's `require` (baseline PLATFORM_MODULES seeds, or a specifier the
+//     manifest declares in dsh.client.external).
 // ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-//
-// 0.1.0-era type surface: the client context type comes from
-// @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime/client, and the ctx.slots Context merge is
-// pulled type-only from @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-slots — the client-runtime
-// split had not happened yet.
